  <details class="bunker-workflow-help" id="bunker-workflow-help">
    <summary>How handover works · roles &amp; terms</summary>
    <h2 id="bunker-workflow-guide" tabindex="-1">Handover workflow</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check — dashboard node admin.</strong> Run health and signing checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Prepare &amp; activate — AWS admin + dashboard node admin.</strong> AWS admin runs the prepare commands; node admin tests the candidate. Only after it passes, AWS admin runs the promotion commands for that exact version.</li>
      <li><strong>Verify &amp; sign off — dashboard node admin.</strong> Test recovery, remove temporary admin access, then confirm the restart and signing test. Attach the four review references and download the report.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>One person may hold both roles. The next-action label names the responsible role; it does not confirm your permissions. The service owner's team can complete the handover without developer AWS access.</p>
    <h3>Version labels</h3>
    <dl class="bunker-terms">
      <dt>Candidate · <code>AWSPENDING</code></dt><dd>Version prepared for testing. The active version stays in use.</dd>
      <dt>Active · <code>AWSCURRENT</code></dt><dd>Version AWS returns by default. Promotion moves this label to the tested candidate; it does not restart the bunker.</dd>
      <dt>Previous · <code>AWSPREVIOUS</code></dt><dd>Former active version. AWS moves this label automatically when the active version changes.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>This rehearsal copies the existing unlock value into a new version. It does not rotate the passphrase or signing key. After promotion, continue to recovery; do not repeat the pending test.</p>
    <h3>Who needs access?</h3>
    <p><strong>Dashboard node admin:</strong> run checks, confirm restart and record acceptance. Dashboard access does not grant AWS permissions.</p>
    <p><strong>AWS admin:</strong> prepare and promote using a separate, scoped AWS profile. The CLI can run off-node. Installing it on the node does not grant access; keep the bunker runtime role read-only.</p>
    <p><strong>Service owner:</strong> owns the handover, IAM review, external-client acceptance and recovery custodian. The node admin records their evidence; developers provide implementation support.</p>
    <p><a href="#bunker-custody-guide" data-bunker-go>AWS access &amp; commands</a> · <a href="#bunker-acceptance-guide" data-bunker-go>Sign-off evidence</a> · <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/whats-in-a-secret.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS version labels</a></p>
    <p>Health shows the latest check. Sign-off records a handover at a point in time; it is not a permanent health guarantee.</p>
  </details>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card" id="bunker-signoff-panel" hidden><h2 id="bunker-acceptance-guide" tabindex="-1">Sign off</h2>
      <p>Accept operational responsibility on behalf of the service owner. Attach the four review references, identifying the delivery provider, accepting operator and recovery custodian in the handover record. Submit to refresh health and record sign-off.</p>
      <form id="bunker-acceptance">
        <label>Effective IAM permissions reviewed<input name="iam_reviewed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-iam-help" placeholder="CHG-2041/iam-review"></label>
        <p id="bunker-iam-help" class="bunker-field-help">IAM review: runtime role, secret policy, KMS and applicable permission limits. Reference the reviewed record.</p>
        <label>Temporary administrator access removed<input name="temporary_admin_removed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-admin-help" placeholder="CHG-2041/admin-removal"></label>
        <p id="bunker-admin-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference removal of temporary grants, credentials and sessions, or a review confirming none remain. Keep the runtime role.</p>
        <h3 id="bunker-external-guide" tabindex="-1">Independent external-client acceptance</h3>
        <label>External client accepted<input name="external_client_accepted" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-external-help" placeholder="UAT-2041/external-client"></label>
        <p id="bunker-external-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference the independent client test: client key, relay, event ID, verified signature and owner acceptance.</p>
        <h3 id="bunker-backup-guide" tabindex="-1">Retained backup and recovery custodian</h3>
        <label>Recovery custodian and retained backup confirmed<input name="recovery_custodian_confirmed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-backup-help" placeholder="OPS-2041/recovery-custody"></label>
        <p id="bunker-backup-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference the retained encrypted backup, integrity check, recovery runbook and named custodian. Test copies are deleted.</p>
        <p>Sign-off refreshes health and checks that the reviewed report is unchanged.</p>
        <button type="submit" class="workspace-button bunker-primary" id="bunker-accept">Sign off</button>
      </form>
      <p id="bunker-acceptance-state"></p>
      <p>Keep the report and supporting records in the handover ticket.</p>
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-export>Export handover evidence</button>
    </article>
